That does not work for the exact same reason many want to descend a
stair case as soon as it is discovered - The initial monsters and items
on the floor are generated when the level is created.  You have confused
randomly generated monsters on a level that has already been cleared
with its initial set of monsters.

Go back up a lot of levels and the monsters will be too weak to help
your experience enough.  Each level takes close to twice as many points
as the previous.  The initial monsters on a level do not advance. 
Randomly created monsters use the average of your current XP and your
current depth.  For an XP=7 player on level 1 any initial monsters left
over are popcorn and newly created monsters are centered around level 4.
That's much too weak to get you up to XP=8 before you need to pray to
avoid starvation.

